1
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:26,000
Kiss your nuts goodbye.

2
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:46,000
Ice Age: The Meltdown is a animation, family, comedy
film directed by Carlos Saldanha.

3
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:06,000
Diego, Manny and Sid return in this sequel to the hit animated movie Ice Age.

4
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:26,000
This time around, the deep freeze is over, and the ice-covered earth is
starting to melt, which will destroy the trio's cherished valley.

5
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:46,000
The impending disaster prompts them to reunite and warn all
the other beasts about the desperate situation.

6
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:06,000
Manny (voice), played by Ray Romano.

7
00:30:20,000 --> 00:30:26,000
Sid (voice), played by John Leguizamo.

8
00:34:40,000 --> 00:34:46,000
Diego (voice), played by Denis Leary.

9
00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:06,000
Ellie (voice), played by Queen Latifah.

10
00:43:20,000 --> 00:43:26,000
Crash (voice), played by Seann William Scott.

11
00:47:40,000 --> 00:47:46,000
Eddie (voice), played by Josh Peck.

12
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:06,000
Ice Age: The Meltdown is a 2006 American animated adventure
comedy film produced by Blue Sky Studios.

13
00:56:20,000 --> 00:56:26,000
The second in the Ice Age film series, it was directed by Carlos Saldanha and features Ray Romano, John Leguizamo, Denis Leary, and Chris
Wedge reprising their roles from the first film, with Seann William Scott, Josh Peck, and Queen Latifah joining the cast.

14
01:00:40,000 --> 01:00:46,000
In the film, Manny, Sid, and Diego attempt to escape an
impending flood, during which Manny finds love.

15
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
Ice Age: The Meltdown premiered on March 19, 2006, at Grauman's Chinese Theater in
Hollywood, and was released in the United States on March 31, by 20th Century Fox.

16
01:09:20,000 --> 01:09:26,000
The film received mixed reviews from critics, and grossed $667
million, becoming the third highest-grossing film of 2006.

17
01:13:40,000 --> 01:13:46,000
Four further follow-ups were released―four sequels of which being Dawn of the Dinosaurs in 2009, Continental
Drift in 2012, and Collision Course in 2016, plus a spin-off, Adventures of Buck Wild in 2022.

18
01:18:00,000 --> 01:18:06,000
A sixth installment, Boiling Point, is set for release in 2027.

19
01:22:20,000 --> 01:22:26,000
The film explores themes of mammoth, sloth, ice age, barrier ice, ice melting.

20
01:26:40,000 --> 01:26:46,000
The tone is lighthearted and thought_provoking.
